            <li><strong>Market Consistency:</strong> The Interquartile Range (IQR) for standard fuels (E10, B7_STANDARD) is relatively tight compared to the absolute spread. This indicates that while extreme outliers exist, the majority of consumers are facing a somewhat consistent pricing band.</li>
            <li><strong>Reporting Compliance:</strong> The median reporting lag is {overall_median_lag:.1f} hours. This suggests that the open data mandate is generally succeeding in providing near real-time pricing to the market. However, the long tail shown in Figure 2 highlights that some retailers are slow to update, which could distort consumer comparison tools.</li>
            <li><strong>Fuel Availability:</strong> Standard diesel (B7_STANDARD) and standard unleaded (E10) are the most widely available fuels, followed by premium grades (E5, B7_PREMIUM). Any policy interventions regarding pricing transparency should primarily target E10 and B7_STANDARD, as these impact the vast majority of motorists.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
"""

